  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Locating objects and places",
     "texto": [
      "To show a location, use prepositions: på («on; in»), under («under»), ved («next to»), mellom («between»), foran («in front of») and bak («behind»). I («in») usually shows that something is inside a space.",
      "På can mean «in» even when there is no horizontal surface, as in på rommet («in the room»). The preposition does not always match English word for word.",
      "Står and ligger describe where something is; they do not always mean that it is literally standing up or lying down. To talk about the location of a place, use ligger."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
